  "limitations_first": [
    "Construction upper bounds only (0 / 6 live 2026-11-17 NIST CSRC wish-list targets solved): InvS-box 33/4/111/14 is +1 gate above Wish-List (c) (G <= 110 at GD <= 14 across both zero-NOT and official NIST %NCFF NOT-permitted models), MixColumns GD = 3 held at 97@3 (Root LP = 92.00) vs Wish-List (e) (<= 93@3), and InvMixColumns GD = 5 held at 118@5 vs Wish-List (f) (G <= 105 at GD <= 5). Wish-List items (a) A <= 27, (b) G <= 100, and (d) MixColumns <= 86 also remain open.",
    "Unbeaten sibling milestones: p1 (InvS-box G <= 104 / S-box G <= 102), p2 (S-box G <= 123 / InvS-box G <= 125 at A = 28), and p4 Route 2 (AD = 3 with A <= 34) remain unbeaten.",
    "Gate-model boundary on NOT-containing files: Milestone p3 (InvMixColumns 92@10) uses pure 2-input {XOR} gates and has zero NOT-gate ambiguity. On [Inv]S-box, usnistgov/Circuits lists aes-invsbox-a55-ad4-g148-gd10-xxn93-26-2.circ.txt (2 NOTs) and aes-sbox-a59-ad4-g159-gd10-xxn100-30-3.circ.txt (3 NOTs), and Joe-b-20 lists aes-invsbox-a47-ad4-g141-gd11-xxn94-44-2.circ.txt (2 NOTs), aes-invsbox-a33-ad4-g121-gd14-xxn88-31-1.circ.txt (1 NOT), and aes-invsbox-a34-ad4-g130-gd13-xxn96-44-1.circ.txt (1 NOT). Note that 33/4/111/14 and 35/4/129/13 achieve strictly fewer total gates than both zero-NOT and NOT-containing baselines at GD <= 14 and GD <= 13 (and T11 proves zero-net-cost unary NOT rewrites on 33/4/111/14 push FWHT depth to 15 > 14), whereas at GD = 10 NIST's 2-NOT 148@10 uses 4 fewer total gates than zero-NOT 152@10.",
    "Solver status distinction (TIMEOUT_UNKNOWN / ITERATION_LIMIT != UNSAT): Full-Zone_Bot 18..21-helper CDCL queries on 105/126/124 (90..120s caps), unconstrained Depth-12 internal cancellations outside 2-sum pools on 33/4/111/14, 3/11 unconstrained 5-layer Zone_Bot K=28 slot-CNF classes on 34/4/111/14, and 29,180-var MixColumns GD=3 CP-SAT G<=93 slices hit TIMEOUT_UNKNOWN / ITERATION_LIMIT and are never claimed as global UNSAT."
  ],
